WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.927
Starlight is a general purpose agent platform.

00:00:02.927 --> 00:00:05.231
You provide the goal and boundaries.

00:00:05.231 --> 00:00:07.722
Your agents provide the implementation.

00:00:07.722 --> 00:00:13.825
Follow real executions through routing, verification, failure, cancellation, and a
remote agent.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:17.908
We begin with three real orders.

00:00:17.908 --> 00:00:22.533
Their amounts are twelve hundred, thirty five hundred, and eight hundred cents.

00:00:22.533 --> 00:00:25.250
The correct total is fifty five hundred cents.

00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:28.430
This deterministic example needs no model or API key.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:33.601
Two agents register different capabilities.

00:00:33.601 --> 00:00:36.144
The order analyst handles structured data.

00:00:36.144 --> 00:00:38.331
The report writer creates documents.

00:00:38.331 --> 00:00:40.519
Each has capacity for one execution.

00:00:40.519 --> 00:00:45.130
Their claims let the coordinator select the appropriate agent for each step.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:51.263
The mission describes an outcome and two ordered steps.

00:00:51.263 --> 00:00:54.702
First summarize the data, then write the verified summary.

00:00:54.702 --> 00:00:57.907
A shared maximum row constraint applies to both steps.

00:00:57.907 --> 00:01:01.170
The platform passes earlier results to the next agent.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:05.500
Now execute the mission.

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:11.078
The coordinator selects the analyst, which computes the total and independently verifies
it.

00:01:11.078 --> 00:01:14.916
The writer then creates a real Markdown file and reads it back.

00:01:14.916 --> 00:01:19.475
Both steps complete, with agent identity, attempts, and evidence recorded.

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:24.062
Inspection reads the saved report.

00:01:24.062 --> 00:01:28.069
The output file contains three orders and fifty five hundred cents.

00:01:28.069 --> 00:01:34.020
A completed status is useful because we can follow it back to a concrete artifact and
its evidence.

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:39.219
Now change only the row limit to one.

00:01:39.219 --> 00:01:41.379
The same source contains three rows.

00:01:41.379 --> 00:01:43.190
The analyst rejects the input.

00:01:43.190 --> 00:01:47.686
The mission fails, the CLI exits with code one, and the writer never starts.

00:01:47.686 --> 00:01:50.255
We assert that no output file was created.

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:55.547
An agent can also claim success incorrectly.

00:01:55.547 --> 00:01:59.453
Here it returns nine thousand nine hundred ninety nine as the total.

00:01:59.453 --> 00:02:03.699
The independent verifier expects fifty five hundred and rejects the claim.

00:02:03.699 --> 00:02:07.435
The platform retains the evidence and does not start the writer.

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:11.967
Next, cancel a running mission.

00:02:11.967 --> 00:02:17.807
The worker observes its abort signal, and the platform prevents the second step from
starting.

00:02:17.807 --> 00:02:19.898
This is cooperative cancellation.

00:02:19.898 --> 00:02:23.955
It cannot forcibly stop arbitrary code or undo external effects.

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:29.042
The same platform also routes to remote Sentinels.

00:02:29.042 --> 00:02:34.589
Here a token authenticated agent connects over a real local WebSocket and counts four
words.

00:02:34.589 --> 00:02:37.572
This capture uses one process with a real socket.

00:02:37.572 --> 00:02:41.270
The repository also includes a separate multi process proof.

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:46.783
Restore the valid input and start a fresh run.

00:02:46.783 --> 00:02:49.861
Both agents complete and verify the artifact again.

00:02:49.861 --> 00:02:51.638
The run has a new identifier.

00:02:51.638 --> 00:02:57.440
This demonstrates recovery by correcting the input, not durable resume or an automatic
rollback.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:05.187
Start with the included example, inspect the reports, then supply your own agents.

00:03:05.187 --> 00:03:08.686
Tools, models, and planning belong inside those agents.

00:03:08.686 --> 00:03:11.123
Starlight coordinates their execution.

00:03:11.123 --> 00:03:17.310
This alpha uses trusted code and in memory history, with clear outcomes and inspectable
evidence.
